Date: Fri, 4 Apr 1997 11:15:03 -0700 (MST)
From: Jon Brinkmann <jb@galileo.apo.nmsu.edu>
Subject: Linux/NT dual boot (Was: Moving to Digtal Alpha system from Intel...)

> 6. how hard is it to install NT 4.0 with Linux simutaneously?

I've been searching for an answer to this one myself.  It is a common
question on this list, and I've not seen an good answer.  The ARC
console will boot either one, but I believe the disk boot blocks
conflict, i.e., you can have only one set of boot code in the boot
sector at a time.  Perhaps someone with dual boot experence can
elaborate on this?

You might be able to run two physical disk drives, one with a Linux
boot block and the other with a NT boot block.  I haven't heard of
anyone trying it.

There is no problem having disk Linux and NT system and user partitions
on the disk simultaneously.  In fact, Linux and NT can share DOS
formatted partitions.

Jon

