From: jestabro@amt.tay1.dec.com
Subject: Re: Linux on AlphaStation 500 
Date: Wed, 09 Apr 1997 11:20:41 +0500

> 
> >>> Komwut Wipusitwarakun said:
> > 
> > I had the problem of loading MILO on my AlphaStation 500 with  
> > one 2-GByte-SCSI-HardDisk, one SCSI-CDROM, one 10-Based-T-Ethernet-Adapter 
> > and one SCSI-Controller(QLogic ISP1020). I used Red Hat Linux/Alpha 4.1 
> > and booted MILO by the \MILO\Alcor\milo image. 
> > 
> > When I boot MILO, I get the following error messages:
> >  "dev_config: don't know to set hostid of SCSI device (1077:1020) " and
> >  "NVRAM is not supported on this system". Then, there are some initialization
> > messages of MILO following with the MILO prompt. I can use some commands such
> > as "set" or "help", but when I try to use the "ls" commamd to access the
> > CDROM , I get the following messages and after that the system is hanged up.
> >  " Ramdisk driver initialized: 16 ramdisks of 4096K size.
> >    Floppy drive(s): fd0 is 2.88M.
> >    floppy0: np floppy controllers found.
> >    qlogicisp: now isp 1020 revision ID(2).
> >    scsi0: QLogic ISP1020 SCSI on PCI bus 0 device 9 irq 28 base 0xb000.
> >    scsi: 1 host. "
> 
> The failure to find a floppy controller and hanging when scanning the SCSI
> bus is usually the result of not receiving any interrupts.
> 
> I assume the AS500 is running the AlphaBIOS console, from which you booted
> MILO? Could you provide me with a log of the hardware configuration, as
> provided by AlphaBIOS, specifically the PCI bus device information?
