Subject: Re: making glibc 2.0.2
In-Reply-To: <Pine.LNX.3.95.970410145539.2629A-100000@balintrc.gardens.udayton.edu>

On Thu, 10 Apr 1997, Woodstock wrote:

> Here's one of the sections that loops forever:
> 
> make[1]: Leaving directory `/tmp/glibc-2.0.2/csu'
> make[1]: Entering directory `/tmp/glibc-2.0.2/csu'
> make[1]: *** File `/usr/include/linux/personality.h' has modification time
> in the future
> make[1]: *** File `/usr/include/linux/ptrace.h' has modification time in
> the future

That's your problem.  Make knows that some object files depend on these
headers, and it will keep re-compiling things until the objects are more
recent than everything they depend on.  If your headers have broken
timestamps then even a newly-compiled file may seem to be older than them.

phil

