> I tried downloading crts.tar.gz from the alphabits directory on redhat,
> and replacing the libgcc.a, which didn't seem to help.  Doing a make
> libgcc.a before compiling anything starts working and then dies on the
> same error.  

You need to replace the crt*.o files as well.  I suspect this is something
you have to think about _before_ you install the new binutils if you want
to do it correctly.  If I remember right, "make libgcc.a" does actually
try to build a new xgcc first, which is doomed to fail.  If I were you I'd
try with the precompiled stuff from alphabits - if that doesn't work you
may need to reinstall an old binutils and take another run at it. 

phil

