Another reason might be because a pointer returned by a syscall such as
"mmap" may *NOT* fit into 32-bits. The Xservers use mmap to map framebuffer
memory into their (user) address space, and the pointers typically end up
being somewhere *above* 0x15500000000UL... :-( (yes, that's 8 zeros) :-(

