> PS--to those of you out there with AXPpci33's with the PS/2-style
> connectors, did your board fit well in normal AT-style cases?  I ordered

 I took to the case with a hack saw and rather enlarged the hole around
the keyboard connector area so both the ps2 mouse and keyboard connectors
were reachable.
 I wasnt going to lose the ablity to use a bus mouse to a small bit of
steel.
 Digital should have done what PC board manufactures to now - bring the
mouse interface out to a pin header like all the other IO connectors.

