NT can run win16 applications and dos applications that do not violate =
NTs security (attempt to access hardware directly) [binary compatible] =
on all NT platforms.  Win32 apps are source compatible on all platforms. =
 Digital has a product FX32 which allows Win32 apps compiled for the =
i386 architecture to run on an alpha (of course with performance =
penalties).

For the Alpha/Linux part of the question,  I am not sure.  But there =
should be ports of the emulators that exist for the Intel/Linux.

